{"name":"Blue Beret","hex":"#40638e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blue Beret","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of blue beret."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blue_Beret"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue beret","blocks":[{"text":"A blue beret is a blue-colored beret used by various military and other organizations. United Nations peacekeepers are often referred to as Blue Berets or Blue Helmets because of their light blue berets or helmets, this includes soldiers, police officers, and civilian personnel. The blue helmet is used as the logo of United Nations Peacekeeping."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/United_Nations_Police_Commissioner_Luis_Carrilho.jpg/330px-United_Nations_Police_Commissioner_Luis_Carrilho.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_beret","wikidata":"Q4142552"},{"title":"Beret","blocks":[{"text":"A beret is a soft, round, flat-crowned cap made of hand-knitted wool, crocheted cotton, wool felt, or acrylic fibre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Sven_Palmqvist_1965.jpg/330px-Sven_Palmqvist_1965.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beret","wikidata":"Q211718"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/UN-Marty.jpg/500px-UN-Marty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/UN-Marty.jpg/500px-UN-Marty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Canadian peacekeeper in 1976 wearing the distinctive UN blue helmet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUN-Marty.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Fashion_Model_in_Hat_%2831553515671%29.jpg/500px-Fashion_Model_in_Hat_%2831553515671%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Fashion_Model_in_Hat_%2831553515671%29.jpg/1280px-Fashion_Model_in_Hat_%2831553515671%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Fashion_Model_in_Hat_%2831553515671%29.jpg/500px-Fashion_Model_in_Hat_%2831553515671%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFashion_Model_in_Hat_(31553515671).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Italian_Soldier_Olypmic_Games_Turin_2006.jpg/500px-Italian_Soldier_Olypmic_Games_Turin_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Italian_Soldier_Olypmic_Games_Turin_2006.jpg/500px-Italian_Soldier_Olypmic_Games_Turin_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u